# Local compose secrets
.env.local

# Runtime state. `var/` holds the billing ledger — an append-only record of what people paid
# and what they spent — so it is both the last thing that should be in a repository and the
# one file on this machine that must survive a restart. The -wal and -shm files are SQLite's
# own; they are the same data mid-write.
var/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Rust build output for the Soroban contracts. `target/` is hundreds of megabytes of
# recompilable artifacts; `Cargo.lock` is NOT here on purpose — a contract is built to be
# deployed byte-for-byte, and the lock file is what makes that reproducible.
target/
*.wasm
